    "narrative": "Our strongest play for today\u2019s slate is undoubtedly **Corbin Carroll**, who leads the team with a robust 78.97 score. Facing Michael McGreevy, **Corbin Carroll** benefits significantly from the mid-4.00 xERA of the opposing starter and a premier lineup spot in the #3 hole, providing the perfect runway for him to leverage his elite sprint speed\u2014our highest priority given the scarcity of stolen bases. Joining him in the \"Strong\" start tier is **Josh Naylor** (65.60), who capitalizes on a favorable matchup against Chandler, bolstered by a strong platoon advantage and a premium #4 spot in the lineup. **Gabriel Moreno** (61.42) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (60.98) also round out our top-tier recommendations, both benefiting from favorable lineup placement and manageable matchups against mid-rotation arms.\n\nNavigating the bench required careful deliberation, particularly regarding **Jose Caballero**. While he just missed the \"Strong\" category with a 56.67 score, his performance is driven by a massive +13% platoon boost against Connelly Early, which keeps him in the starting lineup despite an unfavorable park. The most interesting fringe case was **Seiya Suzuki** (53.53), who remains in the starting mix because of the opportunistic \"Slow SP Delivery\" bonus against Freddy Peralta; even with a sub-optimal BvP history, the potential to swipe a bag off Peralta\u2019s deliberate pace makes him a smarter play than other options. We remain cautious with **James Wood** (52.59); while his xwOBA remains elite, the high-strikeout threat posed by Cristopher S\u00e1nchez forces us to temper expectations. All lineups remain subject to final verification, and we are holding firm on keeping **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Giancarlo Stanton** on the IL while **Mickey Moniak** and **Austin Riley** sit out due to schedule conflicts, leaving prospects like **Carson Williams**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Brice Turang**, and **Trevor Story** to await their turn in the rotation.",
